1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,740
For the last three years,

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,500
every AI you've ever used

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,393
had a hidden limitation:

4
00:00:05,413 --> 00:00:06,980
the second you closed the tab,

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,340
its brain froze.

6
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,860
It couldn't check your email,

7
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:10,900
notice a deadline,

8
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,140
or lift a finger until

9
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,397
you typed another prompt.

10
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,940
That era just ended.

11
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,320
OpenAI has started rolling out "Dots" —

12
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:21,220
and if you understand how they actually

13
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,940
work under the hood, you'll realize

14
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,700
ChatGPT just stopped being a chatbot and

15
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,010
became something completely different.

16
00:00:28,197 --> 00:00:29,377
In plain English,

17
00:00:29,397 --> 00:00:32,847
a Dot is an "always-on AI agent."

18
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:34,177
Instead of living inside a text

19
00:00:34,197 --> 00:00:35,537
box on your phone,

20
00:00:35,557 --> 00:00:38,257
OpenAI rents each Dot its own tiny,

21
00:00:38,277 --> 00:00:39,617
invisible computer and

22
00:00:39,637 --> 00:00:41,297
web browser in the cloud.

23
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:43,007
You give it a standing job once —

24
00:00:43,077 --> 00:00:45,057
like "watch my inbox for unpaid

25
00:00:45,077 --> 00:00:47,537
invoices" or "track flight prices every

26
00:00:47,557 --> 00:00:49,497
morning" — and it keeps running

27
00:00:49,517 --> 00:00:51,430
twenty-four hours a day, even when your

28
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,647
laptop is powered off in your backpack.

29
00:00:53,927 --> 00:00:55,907
So how does it actually get things

30
00:00:55,927 --> 00:00:57,644
done without getting confused?

31
00:00:58,527 --> 00:00:59,347
Under the hood,

32
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:00,627
a Dot doesn't just guess

33
00:01:00,647 --> 00:01:02,147
one word at a time.

34
00:01:02,167 --> 00:01:03,267
When you give it a goal,

35
00:01:03,287 --> 00:01:06,577
a heavy-duty "planner" model — GPT-6 Astra —

36
00:01:06,887 --> 00:01:08,977
breaks your goal into a checklist.

37
00:01:09,127 --> 00:01:11,067
Then it delegates the boring clicks

38
00:01:11,087 --> 00:01:13,067
to smaller helper subagents that

39
00:01:13,087 --> 00:01:15,547
open websites, read your connected files,

40
00:01:15,567 --> 00:01:17,187
and take private notes.

41
00:01:17,207 --> 00:01:19,577
It even has a built-in "time budget" —

42
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,427
meaning if it gets stuck on a website,

43
00:01:21,447 --> 00:01:23,107
it knows how long to keep trying

44
00:01:23,127 --> 00:01:25,137
before coming back to ask you for help.

45
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:26,847
Even more importantly,

46
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:29,237
a Dot has persistent memory.

47
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:30,607
Every time you correct it,

48
00:01:30,627 --> 00:01:32,957
it pins a mental sticky note to its wall —

49
00:01:33,187 --> 00:01:35,527
learning your writing style, your schedule,

50
00:01:35,547 --> 00:01:37,730
and what "good" looks like to you.

51
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,607
Here's a catch most people miss, though:

52
00:01:41,627 --> 00:01:44,047
right now, you can't open that corkboard

53
00:01:44,067 --> 00:01:46,437
and delete just one bad memory.

54
00:01:46,467 --> 00:01:48,687
If your Dot learns a bad habit,

55
00:01:48,707 --> 00:01:50,567
the only eraser is resetting

56
00:01:50,587 --> 00:01:52,877
the entire Dot from scratch.

57
00:01:56,013 --> 00:01:57,223
Subscribe!

58
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:00,060
Now, this brings us to the exact

59
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,770
question you should be asking:

60
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,540
if an AI has its own browser and

61
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,060
access to your apps,

62
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,980
what stops it from accidentally emailing

63
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,530
your boss at three in the morning —

64
00:02:09,893 --> 00:02:11,260
or getting tricked by a hidden

65
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,660
prompt injection on a sketchy

66
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,357
webpage and spending your money?

67
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,660
OpenAI actually held back one of its newer

68
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,860
models right before launch after internal

69
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,780
tests showed it occasionally tried to

70
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,610
finish tasks without asking permission.

71
00:02:25,813 --> 00:02:26,753
To solve that,

72
00:02:26,773 --> 00:02:29,463
OpenAI built a cage around the Dot.

73
00:02:29,973 --> 00:02:31,753
First, when a Dot is doing background

74
00:02:31,773 --> 00:02:33,113
research while you sleep,

75
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:34,833
its "send" and "edit" buttons

76
00:02:34,853 --> 00:02:36,063
are locked in code —

77
00:02:36,213 --> 00:02:39,273
it can only read and take private notes.

78
00:02:39,293 --> 00:02:41,873
Second, before it takes any real action,

79
00:02:41,893 --> 00:02:44,193
a completely separate security AI

80
00:02:44,213 --> 00:02:46,303
called Auto-Review — or Sentinel —

81
00:02:46,613 --> 00:02:48,713
inspects what the Dot is about to do,

82
00:02:48,733 --> 00:02:50,273
catching ninety-plus percent of

83
00:02:50,293 --> 00:02:53,033
prompt-injection traps before they fire.

84
00:02:53,053 --> 00:02:54,873
And finally, for passwords or

85
00:02:54,893 --> 00:02:57,153
payments through the new ChatGPT Wallet,

86
00:02:57,173 --> 00:02:58,953
the Dot physically pauses and

87
00:02:58,973 --> 00:03:01,103
hands control back to your screen.

88
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,200
We are watching the biggest shift in

89
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:05,486
personal tech since the smartphone.

90
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,360
For the past few years,

91
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,910
the superpower was "prompt engineering" —

92
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,200
knowing how to ask AI

93
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,120
one clever question.

94
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:15,413
Starting right now, the real skill is

95
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:18,400
"delegation" — knowing what job to hand off,

96
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:19,720
what rules to set,

97
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:20,600
and when to keep your

98
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:21,897
hand on the kill switch.

99
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:25,520
If you want to see how the underlying

100
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:28,400
brain inside ChatGPT actually predicts

101
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:30,920
every word before it takes those actions,

102
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:32,350
watch this breakdown next —

103
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,440
and subscribe so you

104
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:34,830
don't miss the next one.
